From: "Jose M. Caballero Guerrero"
 <80172778+Caballero-git@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:24:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] arm64: dts: rockchip: P25T: front camera DTB variants

Two new DTBs with the front camera instead of the rear one (one CSI-2
host, one camera at a time):
- rk3566-teclast-p25t-front.dtb: the base DT (USB-C device mode);
- rk3566-teclast-p25t-front-usbhost.dtb: the usbhost DT (USB-C host
  mode), so that a wired keyboard works while the front camera is used.
Both include rk3566-teclast-p25t-front-camera.dtsi: GC02M2 on i2c2 at
0x10, reset GPIO4_B0 (active high), powerdown GPIO4_B3 (active low),
same MCLK, power domain and supplies as the rear GC5035, 1 data lane on
the D-PHY's lanes 2-3 (rockchip,split-lanes-2-3). The rear sensor node
is disabled and its port removed. Values from the stock Android device
tree.

The sensor is mounted turned by 180 degrees (without flips a picture
comes out upside down and mirrored; with both sensor flips it is
upright), described with rotation = <180> so that applications
(libcamera) turn on both flips.

Use one of them in place of rk3566-teclast-p25t.dtb to get the front
camera; the base and usbhost DTBs are unchanged.

P25T tests: p25t-sway tests/ 07-10 (by hand), 11, 20-22.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
